      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-138784",
      ":question/problem": "The architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{\u2032}{B}^{\u2032}{C}^{\u2032}{D}^{\u2032}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{\u2032}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{\u2032}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n           